 What I am confused about is how do I know whether this will span a plane, a line or  $\mathbb{R}^3$ .  
 Does a basis of  $\mathbb{R}^3$  imply it spans  $\mathbb{R}^3$ ? 
 How do I know if a vector spans a plane or a line or  $\mathbb{R}^3$ ?  

Answer: Since there are three variables  $1\over r_x$ ,  $1\over r_y$ ,  $1\over r_z$ , you will need three independent equations for finding them, that is  $$\begin{bmatrix}x_1^2&y_1^2&z_1^2\\ x_2^2&y_2^2&z_2^2\\ x_3^2&y_3^2&z_3^2\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix}{1\over r_x}\\{1\over r_y}\\{1\over r_z}\end{bmatrix}
=\begin{bmatrix}1\\1\\1\end{bmatrix}
$$ 
